1
00:00:05,084 --> 00:00:07,794
(Raj:)Okay, first order
of Physics Bowl business.

2
00:00:08,588 --> 00:00:12,008
(Raj:)We need a truly kick-ass team name.
Suggestions?

3
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:15,555
(Howard:)How about the Perpetual Motion Squad?

4
00:00:15,845 --> 00:00:19,845
(Howard:)It's beyond the laws of physics,
plus a little heads up for the ladies.

5
00:00:20,766 --> 00:00:23,016
- The ladies?
- Perpetual Motion Squad...

6
00:00:23,186 --> 00:00:25,516
(Howard:)...we can go all night.

7
00:00:25,688 --> 00:00:27,568
- I like it.
- I don't.

8
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:30,272
(Sheldon:)Teams are traditionally named after
fierce creatures...

9
00:00:30,443 --> 00:00:32,573
...thus intimidating one's opponent.

10
00:00:32,737 --> 00:00:34,237
We could be the Bengal Tigers.

11
00:00:34,405 --> 00:00:36,365
(Sheldon:)Poor choice. Gram for gram...

12
00:00:36,532 --> 00:00:40,622
(Sheldon:)...no animal exceeds the relative
fighting strength of the army ant.

13
00:00:41,287 --> 00:00:45,457
(Raj:)Maybe so, but you can't incinerate
a Bengal tiger with a magnifying glass.

14
00:00:49,086 --> 00:00:50,166
(Leonard:)Let's put it to a vote.

15
00:00:50,338 --> 00:00:52,168
- All those in favor...
- Point of order.

16
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:54,550
(Sheldon:)I move that any vote on team names
be unanimous.

17
00:00:54,717 --> 00:00:57,847
(Sheldon:)No man should be forced to emblazon
his chest with a Bengal tiger...

18
00:00:58,012 --> 00:01:01,182
(Sheldon:)...when common sense dictates
it should be an army ant.

